`2930-2957`: **Temporary `_matchMethod` property leaks on job objects.**

Line 2934 deletes `_matchedJobSet` but `_matchMethod` (set at lines 2900/2925, read at line 2948) is never cleaned up. Since `submittedJobs` may be polled across multiple iterations of the outer `while` loop, stale `_matchMethod` values from a previous poll cycle could persist and give misleading log output on a subsequent iteration.

<details>
<summary>Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
          const bestMatch = job._matchedJobSet;
          if (!bestMatch) continue;
          delete job._matchedJobSet;
+         const matchMethod = job._matchMethod || 'prompt';
+         delete job._matchMethod;
```

Then at line 2948:

```diff
-                  const matchMethod = job._matchMethod || 'prompt';
+                  // matchMethod already captured above
```
</details>

