`67-86`: **Caption normalization: silent fallback to scene 0 when `startFrame` exceeds total duration.**

If a caption's `startFrame` is beyond the cumulative duration of all scenes, the loop completes without a match and `sceneIdx` defaults to `0`, silently assigning the caption to the first scene. Consider clamping to the last scene or logging a warning.

Also, static analysis flags cyclomatic complexity of 11 (limit 8). Extracting the scene-index-from-frame lookup into a small helper would address that and improve readability.

<details>
<summary>♻️ Suggested helper extraction + last-scene fallback</summary>

